## Phase 1 — ELK Stack on the Monolith

**Goal**: Get centralized structured logging working on the existing monolith before any splitting. Proves the pipeline end-to-end with minimal risk.

### Why First?

- Learn ELK with **one** service, not four
- The `logback-spring.xml` you write here gets copied verbatim into every future microservice
- Immediately useful: searchable logs, error dashboards, request tracing

### Tasks

- [ ] Add `logstash-logback-encoder` dependency to `cinex/pom.xml`
  ```xml
  <dependency>
      <groupId>net.logstash.logback</groupId>
      <artifactId>logstash-logback-encoder</artifactId>
      <version>8.0</version>
  </dependency>
  ```

- [ ] Create `cinex/src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml`
  - Console appender for local dev (human-readable)
  - Logstash TCP appender for Docker profile (structured JSON)
  - Include `service` name, `traceId`, `userId` in every log line

- [ ] Create MDC (Mapped Diagnostic Context) servlet filter
  - New file: `cinex/src/main/java/com/cinex/config/LoggingFilter.java`
  - Extract `userId` from JWT and inject into MDC
  - Generate `traceId` (UUID) per request and inject into MDC
  - These fields automatically appear in every log line

- [ ] Create `logstash/pipeline/logstash.conf`
  - Input: TCP on port `5000` with `json_lines` codec
  - Filter: Parse timestamp, route by service name
  - Output: Index into Elasticsearch as `cinex-{service}-{date}`

- [ ] Add ELK services to `docker-compose.yml`

  | Service | Image | Host Port | Container Port |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Elasticsearch | `elasticsearch:8.15.0` | `9200` | `9200` |
  | Logstash | `logstash:8.15.0` | `5044`, `5000` | `5044`, `5000` |
  | Kibana | `kibana:8.15.0` | `5601` | `5601` |

- [ ] Add `spring.profiles.active=docker` profile for containerized runs
  - `application-docker.properties`: same as dev but with `logstash` host pointing to Docker network name

- [ ] Start full stack, verify logs flow to Kibana
- [ ] Create Kibana index pattern `cinex-*`
- [ ] Write integration test verifying structured log output format

