## Phase 2 — Full Docker Containerization

**Goal**: The entire CineX application (backend + frontend) runs containerized via `docker compose up`. No local Java/Node needed.

### Why Before Jenkins?

Jenkins needs to build Docker images. If your Dockerfiles don't work reliably, Jenkins pipelines will fail. Prove containerization works manually first.

### Tasks

- [ ] Verify existing `cinex/Dockerfile` works end-to-end
  - Build: `docker build -t cinex-backend ./cinex`
  - Run: connects to Dockerized Postgres, Redis, Logstash
  - Fix any issues (timezone, profile activation, health checks)

- [ ] Create `cineX_Frontend/Dockerfile`
  ```dockerfile
  # Build stage
  FROM node:22-alpine AS build
  WORKDIR /app
  COPY package*.json ./
  RUN npm ci
  COPY . .
  RUN npm run build

  # Serve stage
  FROM nginx:alpine
  COPY --from=build /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
  COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
  EXPOSE 80
  ```

- [ ] Create `cineX_Frontend/nginx.conf`
  - Serve static files
  - Proxy `/api/*` requests to the backend service
  - Handle SPA routing (fallback to `index.html`)

- [ ] Add `cinex-backend` and `cinex-frontend` services to `docker-compose.yml`

  | Service | Build Context | Host Port |
  |---|---|---|
  | cinex-backend | `./cinex` | `9090` |
  | cinex-frontend | `./cineX_Frontend` | `80` |

- [ ] Test full stack: `docker compose up --build`
  - Frontend loads at `http://localhost`
  - API calls proxy through Nginx to backend
  - Logs flow to Kibana
  - Metrics scraped by Prometheus

### New Files

```
CineX/
├── cineX_Frontend/
│   ├── Dockerfile                [NEW]
│   └── nginx.conf                [NEW]
```

### Verification

- `docker compose up --build -d` → all 10+ containers start and become healthy
- Browse `http://localhost` → frontend loads, login works
- Browse `http://localhost:5601` → Kibana shows backend logs
- Browse `http://localhost:3030` → Grafana shows JVM metrics
