## Phase 7 — Dashboards + Alerting

**Goal**: Production-grade visibility and automated alerts.

### Kibana Dashboards (Logs)

| Dashboard | Purpose | Filters |
|---|---|---|
| **Error Overview** | All ERROR logs across services, grouped by service | `level:ERROR`, split by `service` |
| **Request Trace** | Follow a single request across all services | Filter by `traceId` |
| **Booking Flow** | Booking lifecycle: initiate → lock → confirm → notify | `service:booking-service` + `service:notification-service` |
| **Auth Activity** | Login attempts, failures, registration trends | `service:auth-service`, `message:*login*` |

### Grafana Dashboards (Metrics)

| Dashboard | Data Source | Panels |
|---|---|---|
| **JVM Overview** | Prometheus | Heap usage, GC pauses, thread count per service |
| **RED Metrics** | Prometheus | Request Rate, Error Rate, Duration (p50/p95/p99) per endpoint |
| **Database Pool** | Prometheus | HikariCP active/idle connections per service |
| **Redis** | Prometheus | Active seat locks, connection pool, command latency |

### Alerting (No Custom Service Needed)

| Alert | Tool | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Service down | Prometheus Alertmanager | `up == 0` for any service for > 30s |
| Error rate spike | Prometheus Alertmanager | `rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{status=~"5.."}[5m]) > 0.05` |
| Booking failures | Grafana Alert | Payment verify errors > 3 in 5 min |
| Log error flood | Kibana Alerting | > 10 ERROR logs from any single service in 1 min |
| Disk space | Prometheus Alertmanager | Elasticsearch disk usage > 80% |

